C%22%20height%3D%5C%222668%5C%22%3E%3Cfigcaption%3EDario%20Amodei%2C%20CEO%20of%20Anthropic%3Cp%3EBloomberg%2FGetty%20Images%3C%2Fp%3E%3C%2Ffigcaption%3E%3C%2Ffigure%3E%3Cul%3E%3Cli%3EJacob%20Coxon's%20Anthropic%20exit%20sparked%20debate%20over%20whether%20to%20push%20for%20AI%20safety%20from%20inside%20or%20out.%3C%2Fli%3E%3Cli%3EThe%20resignation%20also%20drew%20scrutiny%20over%20its%20impact%20on%20Anthropic's%20image%20and%20upcoming%20IPO.%3C%2Fli%3E%3Cli%3EAI%20workers'%20stay-or-go%20conundrum%20has%20a%20World%20War%20II%20parallel%2C%20a%20tech%20historian%20says.%3C%2Fli%3E%3C%2Ful%3E%3Cp%3EAI%20workers%20with%20apocalypse%20fears%20are%20facing%20a%20troubling%2C%20though%20not%20unprecedented%2C%20%3Ca%20href%3D%5C%22https%3A%2F%2Fwww.businessinsider.com%2Fanthropic-researcher-quits-over-ai-safety-concerns-2026-9%5C%22%20target%3D%5C%22_blank%5C%22%3Ecareer%20dilemma%3C%2Fa%3E.%3C%2Fp%3E%3Cp%3EShould%20they%20quit%20their%20jobs%20to%20avoid%20potentially%20helping%20make%20the%20doomsday%20scenario%20they%20envision%20a%20reality%3F%20Or%2C%20should%20they%20drive%20change%20for%20the%20better%20from%20within%3F%3C%2Fp%3E%3Cp%3EIt's%20a%20thorny%20predicament%20that%20came%20into%20focus%20this%20week%20when%20Jacob%20Coxon%2C%20a%20former%20OpenAI%20employee%2C%20said%20in%20an%20X%20post%20that%20he%20was%20resigning%20from%20Anthropic%20because%20the%20%26quot%3Bpeople%20building%20AI%20earnestly%20believe%20that%20it%20could%20kill%20us%20all%20by%20the%20end%20of%20the%20decade.%26quot%3B%3C%2Fp%3E%3Cp%3ESoon%20after%2C%20Evan%20Hubinger%2C%20who%20leads%20Anthropic's%20alignment%20stress-testing%20team%2C%20essentially%20backed%20Coxon%2C%20saying%20he%20believes%20there%20is%20a%20%3Ca%20href%3D%5C%22https%3A%2F%2Fwww.businessinsider.com%2Fopenai-safety-hire-people-die-lose-control-ai-paul-christiano-2026-9%5C%22%20target%3D%5C%22_blank%5C%22%3Egreater-than-10%25%20chance%20AI%20could%20kill%3C%2Fa%3E%20all%20humans%20within%20the%20next%20decade.%3C%2Fp%3E%3Ch2%20data-toc-id%3D%5C%22eb8b4adb-8f6e-45d0-a998-51d6925c65fc%5C%22%3EWhy%20some%20workers%20stay%3C%2Fh2%3E%3Cp%3EFor%20AI%20workers%20worried%20that%20they're%20contributing%20to%20mankind's%20destruction%2C%20deciding%20whether%20to%20quit%20or%20stay%20put%20is%20more%20complicated%20than%20it%20may%20seem%2C%20said%20Jeremie%20Harris%2C%20CEO%20and%20cofounder%20of%20Gladstone%20AI%2C%20a%20Washington%2C%20DC-based%20safety%20and%20advisory%20company%20focused%20on%20national%20security%20risks%20and%20%3Ca%20href%3D%5C%22https%3A%2F%2Fwww.businessinsider.com%2Fhow-ai-could-kill-humanity-chatbot-responses-2026-9%5C%22%20target%3D%5C%22%5C%22%3Ecatastrophic%20threats%3C%2Fa%3E%20from%20advanced%20AI.%20%26quot%3BI%20don't%20particularly%20fault%20anyone%20for%20making%20either%20call%2C%26quot%3B%20he%20said.%3C%2Fp%3E%3Cp%3EHarris%20said%20his%20job%20involves%20regularly%20talking%20with%20staff%20at%20Anthropic%20and%20other%20top%20AI%20labs%2C%20and%20that%20in%20recent%20months%20he's%20heard%20many%20express%20fears%20similar%20to%20those%20Coxon%20described.%20While%20quitting%20can%20be%20a%20moral%20response%20to%20building%20a%20%3Ca%20href%3D%5C%22https%3A%2F%2Fwww.businessinsider.com%2Fsmart-people-react-openai-hugging-face-hacking-cybersecurity-incident-2026-7%2520Mind%2520adding%3F%C2%A0(edited)%5C%22%20target%3D%5C%22%5C%22%3Edangerous%20technology%3C%2Fa%3E%2C%20he%20said%2C%20Al%20labs%20could%20end%20up%20with%20few%20or%20no%20workers%20willing%20to%20press%20for%20change%20if%20resignations%20pile%20up.%3C%2Fp%3E%3Cp%3E%26quot%3BThe%20people%20who%20are%20left%20are%20going%20to%20be%20the%20ones%20who%20are%20least%20concerned%20about%20safety%2C%26quot%3B%20Harris%20said%2C%20while%20%26quot%3Bpeople%20who%20care%20arguably%20should%20be%20the%20ones%20in%20the%20seat.%26quot%3B%3C%2Fp%3E%3Cp%3EIn%20response%20to%20Coxon's%20announcement%2C%20Anthropic%20employee%20Anna%20Wang%20said%20on%20X%20that%20she%20works%20at%20the%20company%20because%20she%20thinks%20she%20%26quot%3Bcan%20do%20better%20at%20reducing%20risks%20from%20the%20inside.%26quot%3B%20She%20added%20that%20she%20respects%20and%20endorses%20others%20%26quot%3Bwho%20think%20that%20it's%20better%20to%20do%20so%20from%20the%20outside.%26quot%3B%3C%2Fp%3E%3Cp%3EA%20spokesperson%20for%20Anthropic%20declined%20to%20comment%20after%20confirming%20Wang's%20employment.%3C%2Fp%3E%3Cp%3ECoxon's%20X%20post%2C%20which%20also%20sparked%20online%20debate%20over%20its%20impact%20on%20Anthropic's%20image%2C%20the%20company's%20%3Ca%20href%3D%5C%22https%3A%2F%2Fwww.businessinsider.com%2Fanthropic-1-5-trillion-valuation-on-secondary-markets-2026-8%5C%22%20target%3D%5C%22%5C%22%3Ecoming%20IPO%3C%2Fa%3E%2C%20and%20the%20possibility%20that%20this%20is%20all%20a%20strange%20publicity%20stunt%2C%20echoes%20concerns%20of%20a%20pending%20AI%20calamity%20previously%20made%20by%20Geoffrey%20Hinton%2C%20the%20%3Ca%20href%3D%5C%22https%3A%2F%2Fwww.businessinsider.com%2Fgodfather-ai-geoffrey-hinton-on-ai-sad-dangerous-2026-1%5C%22%20target%3D%5C%22_blank%5C%22%3Ecomputer%20scientist%3C%2Fa%3E%20widely%20known%20as%20the%20%26quot%3BGodfather%20of%20AI%2C%26quot%3B%20xAI%20founder%20Elon%20Musk%2C%20and%20others.%3C%2Fp%3E%3Cp%3EThe%20general%20public%20is%20apprehensive%20about%20AI%2C%20too.%20Some%2052%25%20of%20Americans%20are%20more%20concerned%20than%20excited%20about%20the%20use%20of%20the%20technology%20in%20daily%20life%2C%20according%20to%20a%20June%20study%20from%20the%20Pew%20Research%20Center.%20That's%20up%20from%2037%25%20who%20said%20the%20same%20in%202021.%3C%2Fp%3E%3Ch2%20data-toc-id%3D%5C%22a15ae389-0a55-4b3d-b169-4349b2f84fb9%5C%22%3EA%20dilemma%20with%20a%20history%3C%2Fh2%3E%3Cp%3EFor%20AI%20workers%20who%20truly%20believe%20their%20employer%20is%20creating%20an%20existential%20threat%2C%20Alex%20Wellerstein%2C%20a%20professor%20at%20Stevens%20Institute%20of%20Technology%2C%20said%20internal%20voices%20of%20reason%20have%20a%20poor%20track%20record%20of%20%26quot%3Bovercoming%20preexisting%20institutional%20momentum.%26quot%3B%3C%2Fp%3E%3Cp%3E%26quot%3BIf%20you%20stick%20around%2C%20you're%20participating%2C%26quot%3B%20he%20said.%3C%2Fp%3E%3Cp%3EThat%20tension%20is%20not%20new.%20Technology%20historian%20Matthew%20H.%20Hersch%20said%20%3Ca%20href%3D%5C%22https%3A%2F%2Fwww.businessinsider.com%2Foppenheimer-los-alamos-manhattan-project-scientists-atomic-bomb-petition-2023-7%5C%22%20target%3D%5C%22%5C%22%3Ethe%20Manhattan%20Project%3C%2Fa%3E%2C%20a%20World%20War%20II-era%20program%20to%20develop%20nuclear%20weapons%2C%20is%20a%20close%20parallel.%3C%2Fp%3E%3Cp%3ERalph%20Austin%20Bard%2C%20then%20undersecretary%20of%20the%20US%20Navy%2C%20privately%20urged%20officials%20to%20warn%20Japan%20before%20using%20%3Ca%20href%3D%5C%22https%3A%2F%2Fwww.businessinsider.com%2Fwhat-hiroshima-looks-like-today-photos%5C%22%20target%3D%5C%22%5C%22%3Ethe%20atomic%20bomb%3C%2Fa%3E%20and%20resigned%20weeks%20before%20Hiroshima%2C%20likely%20in%20protest%20of%20the%20decision%20not%20to%20do%20so%2C%20said%20Hersch%2C%20also%20a%20professor%20at%20Harvard%20University%20and%20a%20member%20of%20the%20School%20of%20Historical%20Studies%20at%20the%20Institute%20for%20Advanced%20Study.%3C%2Fp%3E%3Cp%3EOther%20Manhattan%20Project%20scientists%20also%20unsuccessfully%20pushed%20for%20a%20demonstration%20of%20the%20bomb%20before%20it%20was%20used%20in%20combat%2C%20some%20of%20whom%20were%20effectively%20barred%20from%20future%20defense%20work%2C%20he%20added.%3C%2Fp%3E%3Cp%3E%26quot%3BWhistleblowers%20can%20do%20tremendous%20good%2C%26quot%3B%20Hersch%20told%20Business%20Insider%2C%20%26quot%3Bbut%20are%20apt%20to%20be%20discredited%20or%20harassed%20into%20silence%2C%20and%20become%20unemployable%20in%20their%20industry.%26quot%3B%3C%2Fp%3E%3Cdiv%3ERead%20the%20original%20article%20on%20%3Ca%20href%3D%5C%22https%3A%2F%2Fwww.businessinsider.com%2Fai-apocalypse-workers-fearing-face-thorny-career-dilemma-2026-9%5C%22%3EBu